From 4935a42151d295561a0416af7e01cb89439d4a9a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 05:08:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Speed S2-11 (GBA house): the restore's row loops run from the
 IWRAM room group

The busy Live layout (room-test 1, 4 chibis) already restores one rect per walker
(3-5 rects, about 700 px each a tick); the time went to the per-row control code
of those rects running as THUMB from ROM (about 3 cycles an instruction). Moved to
ARM in the IWRAM overlay's room group (the slot is the 3D group's 10,352 B; the
room group grows 3,588 -> 7,452 B inside it, no resident byte): the shell's row
loop (shell_rows), wall_rows, floor_row, row_copy, the pieces' runs (runs_plain,
runs_lut) and block_sum. Same code, same pixels.

GBA speed2 house (before -> after): live, 4 chibis 26.8 fps / 32.4 ms avg / 47.7
max / 27 frames at 3 vblanks -> 30.0 / 25.7 / 35.5 / none; defend siege wave 3
29.5 fps / 31.4 ms / 4 frames at 3 vblanks -> 30.0 / 26.6 / none; test-home
home_steady 29.2 -> 30.0 fps (work 29.8 -> 24.3 ms). Frame hashes of every tick
of speed2_house (2,296 frames, sync on) equal the base ROM's except the first
1-3 frames after the three scene loads, where SP5's load fade (a register, by
real vblanks) is at another level because the load is shorter. test-home's 108
room-parity checks pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RLcGbHBa2kju7ynbaJLHT6
